# Keeps the build context small and keeps secrets and patient data out of image
# layers.
#
# Scope, stated plainly because it is easy to get wrong: Docker reads the
# .dockerignore found in the root of the BUILD CONTEXT. The compose stack builds
# with `context: ./backend` and `context: ./frontend`, so this file does NOT
# filter those two builds. It applies when the repository root is the context —
# `docker build .`, a CI image, an `ADD`-style archive of the tree.
#
# The two Dockerfiles therefore do not rely on it: each COPYs its source trees
# by name instead of using `COPY . .`, which is what actually keeps a
# developer's .env, .venv, var/ or sample scans out of the images.

# --- version control and CI ------------------------------------------------ #
.git
.gitignore
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml

# --- secrets --------------------------------------------------------------- #
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json

# --- patient data and calibration output ----------------------------------- #
var/
backend/var/
samples/
scans/
uploads/
calibration.csv
benchmark.json
*.pdf
*.tif
*.tiff

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------- #
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# --- Node ------------------------------------------------------------------ #
# node_modules is excluded so `npm ci` runs against the lockfile inside the
# image rather than copying a host tree built for a different platform.
**/node_modules
# dist is excluded so the image always contains a bundle built in this build,
# not a stale one from a developer's machine.
frontend/dist
dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*

# --- docs and local artefacts, not needed at runtime ------------------------ #
docs/
ops/
Makefile
docker-compose*.yml
README.md
**/*.log
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/celerybeat-schedule*

# --- editors and operating systems ----------------------------------------- #
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
